    "explanation": "The $4.00 cancellation fee is refunded to the rider in full. The deciding fact is the driver's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-00201, 98 driver fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps): it never brings the vehicle closer than 779.93 m to the pickup pin at Blk 118 Rivervale Drive, and records zero fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius. POL-NS-01 makes the fee chargeable only if the trace places the driver inside the pickup geofence at or before the 'arrived' event; that limb fails on the driver's own telemetry, as the Driver Advocate properly and candidly conceded, and the dwell limb fails with it (0 seconds against the 300-second minimum). POL-NS-02, POL-NS-05 and POL-NS-06 each reach the same result independently, and POL-NS-04 exonerates the rider as well. POL-NS-03 does not rescue the fee: that clause covers a driver stationary within 400 m of the pin at the wrong face of the venue, and this driver was never within 779 m, so the 400 m ceiling is never met and no pin-ambiguity goodwill payment arises. On the rider's side, POL-NS-04 is satisfied on all three limbs: the rider sent a locating message at 08:05:33 naming the block and saying he could not see the vehicle, the driver posted no reply and made no in-app call before cancelling, and the rider track (122 fixes, maximum 24.9 m from the pin, zero fixes filtered for accuracy) places him inside the 100 m presence radius for every qualifying fix. The 'arrived' marker at 08:02:14 is a false arrival marker under POL-NS-05: at that timestamp the driver was hundreds of metres outside the 300 m threshold, so the marker does not start the waiting clock, and because there is no qualifying in-geofence fix anywhere in the trip, POL-NS-05(ii) refunds the fee in full and directs the false-arrival record carried in the referrals list. No driver compensation is payable: POL-NS-07 operates only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, which it is not, and in any event the anti-farming check on driver